content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-103, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22410, filtered-water line",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end housing vibration is exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS. The applicable Figure 3 threshold is the Zone C/Zone D boundary at 7.1: Zone C (4.5–7.1 mm/s RMS) is 'Restricted—plan maintenance', while Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS) is 'Damage likely—stop the pump'. Figure 3 expressly does not establish which zone owns a value exactly on the boundary, so a definitive zone classification cannot be made. Apply the more restrictive stop-and-notify response as an interim P1 precaution, not as a claim that 7.1 is conclusively Zone D.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Housing temperature is 72°C. The HF-300 bearing-housing limits are normal up to 70°C, alarm at 80°C and trip at 90°C, with temperature measured on the housing surface. Thus 72°C is 2°C above the normal limit, but 8°C below alarm and 18°C below trip. The site requirement for a priority-1 work order based on temperature above the manufacturer's alarm limit is not triggered; the elevated temperature still supports checks of grease quantity, bearings and alignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leak is reported. The manual's shaft-seal leakage symptom does not therefore provide a basis for automatic seal replacement. Seal work and associated parts below are conditional on a separately confirmed need; the high-vibration and elevated-bearing-temperature troubleshooting rows are the applicable rows for the reported condition.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Misalignment: listed as a probable cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature, making it a leading common explanation for the two abnormal readings. Check alignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear: also common to the manual's high-vibration and high-bearing-temperature causes. Inspect the bearings and replace them if worn.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing: a documented cause of high bearing temperature and therefore a possible contributor to the 72°C housing reading. Check grease quantity.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage: a documented cause of high vibration. Inspect the impeller before deciding whether any impeller repair or replacement is needed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation: a documented cause of high vibration. Check NPSH; the report contains no NPSH or cavitation measurements.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Stop P-103 immediately if it is running and keep it stopped under the interim conservative response to the unresolved 7.1 mm/s RMS boundary reading. Notify the reliability engineer before any restart. Record that the exact zone remains unresolved rather than entering an unsupported Zone C or Zone D classification.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before internal pump or seal work, electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; and obtain a line-break permit, draining and venting first. Use the required chemical PPE during the work.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Diagnose the reported condition by checking alignment, inspecting the bearings and impeller, checking NPSH, and checking bearing grease quantity. Record all findings and measurements so the actual cause and released corrective scope can be established.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If rotating-assembly removal is needed for access, use the HF-300 back pull-out arrangement, which permits removal without disturbing the casing or pipework. The assembly weighs 68 kg, so use a signed lifting plan and certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace bearings if inspection confirms wear. Correct other causes only on the basis of the inspection and alignment/NPSH findings; the evidence does not establish impeller replacement or seal replacement as routine scope for this report.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If seal replacement is separately confirmed as necessary, do not fit HF3-450. Fit pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B, which requires no sleeve measurement for seal setting, and tighten its gland nuts to 30 Nm. Inspect shaft sleeve HF3-455 for scoring and replace it if scoring depth exceeds 0.1 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "On reassembly, replace casing gasket HF3-120 whenever the casing has been opened. For disturbed manual Table 5 fasteners with lightly oiled threads, use: M16 casing bolts 210 Nm, M24 impeller nut 160 Nm, and M12 bearing-housing bolts 85 Nm. Use 30 Nm rather than the manual's superseded 25 Nm for HF3-450B seal gland nuts.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before restart, confirm that the reliability engineer has been notified and that the interim stop has been dispositioned. Maintain the Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After return to service, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings every week and classify the highest reading using Figure 3. Continue checking housing-surface temperature against the 70°C normal, 80°C alarm and 90°C trip limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C02",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; conditional on inspection identifying drive-end bearing replacement as required.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; conditional on inspection identifying non-drive-end bearing replacement, or an authorized bearing-pair replacement, as required.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; required whenever the casing is opened, otherwise not released for this work.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Pre-set cartridge mechanical seal; conditional on a confirmed seal-replacement scope. This is the required seal for this serial range; do not substitute HF3-450.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve; conditional on seal-related inspection finding scoring deeper than 0.1 mm.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "For any work inside the pump or on its seal: electrical isolation and lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves; and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "P-103 is within P-101 to P-106 on the chemically dosed filtered-water line, using sodium hypochlorite. Wear chemical goggles and nitrile gloves for work on the line.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "For lifting the 68 kg back pull-out assembly, which exceeds the site's 25 kg threshold, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The site requires immediate stopping and notification of the reliability engineer before restart for vibration in the manufacturer's highest severity zone. Because exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS is the unresolved boundary into that zone, apply this response conservatively until the classification is dispositioned.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Maintain Plan 11 seal flush from pump discharge and never run the pump seal dry.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard labour allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional bearing replacement, pair: standard labour allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, released only if the inspection establishes that bearing-pair replacement is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Conditional mechanical seal replacement: standard labour allowance 4.0 hours with 2 technicians. This is not released solely on the current report because no leak is reported; it applies only if a separate seal-replacement need is confirmed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "The manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450, and manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm for seal gland nuts. Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, instead requires HF3-450B and 30 Nm for HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward. P-103 is serial HF3-22410 and is therefore inside the bulletin's serial range; the below-HF3-22000 exception does not apply. For any seal work on this asset, SB-2026-014 governs: use HF3-450B, use 30 Nm, and do not use the manual's HF3-450/25 Nm instructions.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Figure 3 and SSP-07 do not conflict on the required Zone D response, but they do not resolve the exact-boundary classification: Figure 3 touches Zones C and D at 7.1 and expressly leaves boundary ownership unspecified, while SSP-07's mandatory stop applies to the highest severity zone. The interim stop is therefore a conservative work-order control; the technical zone classification remains an open question.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Does exactly 7.1 mm/s RMS belong to Figure 3 Zone C or Zone D for this pump, and what restart criteria apply? C07 expressly does not define boundary ownership; reliability engineering or AquaDyne must disposition this before the interim conservative classification is changed.",
    "What is the non-drive-end housing vibration reading? Only the drive-end value was reported, while C06 requires measurement on both bearing housings and classification of the highest reading.",
    "What are the alignment results, bearing condition, grease quantity, impeller condition and NPSH/cavitation findings? The evidence does not establish the root cause or determine which conditional bearing, impeller-related or other corrective work is required.",
    "If the seal area is opened for a separately confirmed reason, what is the shaft-sleeve scoring depth? No measurement is supplied against the SB-2026-014 replacement criterion of scoring exceeding 0.1 mm depth.",
    "What labour is required for diagnosis, grease and NPSH checks, internal inspection and any impeller work? C12 supplies standard times only for mechanical-seal replacement, bearing-pair replacement and laser alignment, so a total job duration cannot be fixed from the evidence."
  ]
}
